# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml and
# .github/workflows/semver-label.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does.
#
# Product (deliberately NOT listed): Go source, go.mod/go.sum, Dockerfile +
# .dockerignore, example config, README.md, LICENSE.

# CI and agent instructions
/.github/
/.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/CONTRIBUTING*

# Docs: not in the image
/docs/

# Tests
*_test.go
testdata/

# Dev build wrapper (the Dockerfile and release call go build directly)
/Makefile

# Linter / formatter / git config
/.golangci*
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.editorconfig
/.gitignore
